    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Description\n\nhttps://github.com/neovim/nvim-lspconfig/blob/43ed3797b266e1ee8d222e491379ad471c9d3146/lsp/denols.lua#L107-L126\n\nI just check the code, find now denols require always be used for a project dir, and nowadays we can also not control the root_marks, I wonder if it is by design",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "I have read the pr for it.. I do not think it is a clever fix for it. Before we can control the root_mark for them. but now there is not setting place for root_mark. But we can also choose if to enable them or not in our config, reading the root files in our config. Now it become a bug that event I write enable in the config, the lsp still cannot enable. Then it becomes a really bug I think\n\nThis is my solution in my config\n\nhttps://github.com/Decodetalkers/nvim.dot/blob/next-lsp/lua/cmps/cmps_setup.lua#L161-L182\n\nI think the fix for that is not a good fix, not to mention that deno also support package.json ad root mark",
